-- title:
--   Smooth B-invariant functions generated by one non-constant vector
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $G = \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$. Let $S$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of the space of all functions $G \to \mathbb{C}$ which is stable under right translation, i.e. for every $h \in G$ and every $F \in S$ the function $g \mapsto F(gh)$ again lies in $S$. Suppose $S$ contains a function $F_0$ which is locally constant, invariant under left multiplication by the elements $b \in G$ whose underlying matrix has lower-left entry $(b)_{1,0} = 0$ (so $F_0(bg) = F_0(g)$ for all such $b$ and all $g$), and non-constant in the precise sense that $F_0(g) \neq F_0(1)$ for some $g \in G$. Then every function $F : G \to \mathbb{C}$ which is locally constant and satisfies $F(bg) = F(g)$ for all $g \in G$ and all $b \in G$ with $(b)_{1,0} = 0$ belongs to $S$. No continuity, smoothness or finiteness assumption is imposed on $S$ itself beyond right-translation stability.
--
--   The locally constant functions on $G$ invariant under left multiplication by the upper-triangular Borel subgroup form the smooth induction of the trivial character of $B$, whose only right-translation-invariant subspaces are $0$, the constants and the whole space, the quotient by the constants being the Steinberg representation; the statement is that form of this irreducibility assertion in which the ambient space of functions is an arbitrary translation-stable submodule. It is used in the analysis of principal-series carriers, via [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier.exists_forall_stable_iff_of_hasCharConductor_of_ratio_eq_natCast`](thm.html#LocalNewvector.PSCarrier.exists_forall_stable_iff_of_hasCharConductor_of_ratio_eq_natCast), and the proof invokes the Iwasawa decomposition $G = B \cdot \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}_p)$ together with the production of indicator functions of Borel cells inside $S$.
